---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/Briefing.css';
---

<Layout title="ORION // OP 2: The Quiet Line - Briefing" description="Field briefing for Operation The Quiet Line - Korpiharju ridge, Zone-21 Finland." nav={[{ href: '/orion-fimbulwinter/mission-control/', label: '<- MISSION CONTROL' }, { href: '#situation', label: 'SITUATION' }, { href: '#mission', label: 'MISSION' }, { href: '#ground', label: 'GROUND' }, { href: '#execution', label: 'EXECUTION' }, { href: '#roe', label: 'ROE' }, { href: '#support', label: 'SUPPORT' }]} footer="ORION INTERNATIONAL - ZONE-21 // FIMBULWINTER - OP 2: THE QUIET LINE - BRIEFING" decryptLines={['ORION SECURE UPLINK - CHANNEL 21', 'AUTHENTICATING OPERATOR...', 'CLEARANCE CONFIRMED - FIELD COMMAND', 'DECRYPTING DOSSIER: OPERATION THE QUIET LINE']}>
  <div class="briefing-actions"><button class="print-opord" type="button">PRINT OPORD</button></div>
  <section id="situation" class="briefing-section"><h1 class="op-name">SITUATION</h1><h2 class="op-title">OPERATION THE QUIET LINE</h2><div class="reveal"><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Four days after Signal Fire, the 44th Army Corps' main body is across the border and moving past Ahola toward the next FDF line. The village is behind them now. Whatever got out, got out.</p><div class="annotated"><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">The corps runs this whole sector on wire and short-hop UHF. No satellite links worth intercepting, no drones - every tasking, every fire request, every convoy serial passes through a handful of ground relay nodes. The hardened one for this sector sits on the forest ridge northwest of Ahola that the locals call Korpiharju. <span class="intel-source">[SOURCE: ORION SIGINT - RELIABILITY A-2]</span></p><aside class="margin-note note-a">don't break it - borrow it</aside></div><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">It is not a soft relay post. It is dug in, wired, mined, garrisoned, with a QRF on short call from the sluice road. Flattening it achieves little - a backup node picks up the traffic within the hour, and a dead hub tells the corps only that something is wrong, not what.</p><div class="annotated"><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Orion wants one transmission through it: a single order, in the corps' own format, that the whole sector net will believe. That requires the current cryptographic key set. The keys live with the corps Chief of Signals, Colonel Arkady Volkov, who rotates them on a fixed schedule and is forward on the ridge this week to run the handover himself. <span class="intel-source">[SOURCE: FDF LIAISON - RELIABILITY B-2]</span> <span class="intel-warning">WINDOW CLOSES ON ROTATION - FIELD VERIFICATION REQUIRED</span></p><aside class="margin-note note-b">one night, one set of keys</aside></div><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Chernov has a resupply and reinforcement convoy staged to move through this sector and mass against the FDF line. That convoy moves on orders authenticated through the Korpiharju net. One properly keyed transmission decides where it spends the night.</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">A freelance journalist, Nieminen, is still working the region. Orion is still not here officially.</p></div></section>
  <section id="mission" class="briefing-section"><h2 class="op-name">MISSION</h2><h3 class="op-title">TASKING</h3><div class="intel reveal"><div class="head">FIELD COMMAND DIRECTIVE</div><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Orion elements will intercept Colonel Volkov and recover the 44th's current sector key set intact; assault and hold the Korpiharju communications hub long enough to seize its transmitter and signals log intact; and transmit one authenticated false order over the corps net to divert the staged convoy off its planned axis.</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">On completion Orion will break contact west off the ridge before the sector QRF closes the egress.</p></div></section>
  <section id="ground"><h2 class="op-name">GROUND</h2><h3 class="op-title">FIELD NAVIGATION</h3><div class="intel reveal"><div class="head">TERRAIN // KORPIHARJU SECTOR</div><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">A forest road and a corps forward CP northeast of the ridge (Phase 1). The fortified comms hub on the Korpiharju high ground itself (Phases 2-3). A farmstead line and a level crossing on the west side for exfil (Phase 5).</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll" style="color:var(--dim);font-size:12px;">Tactical overlay to follow once Eden placement is locked. Phase positions above are directional, not gridded.</p></div></section>
  <section id="execution" class="briefing-section"><h2 class="op-name">EXECUTION</h2><h3 class="op-title">ORDER OF BATTLE</h3><div><div class="phase reveal" id="execution-phase-1" data-phase="1"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="1" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">PHASE 1 / 5</div><h3>Take the Keys</h3><div class="annotated"><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Intercept Colonel Volkov as he moves between the corps forward CP and the ridge with a small security detail. Recover the fill device and codebook intact - damaged key material fails the operation's purpose. Keep it quiet: if the corps registers him lost or the keys compromised before Phase 4, they rotate early and the transmission is worthless. Ground element chooses the ambush on the move or a hit on the forward CP.</p><aside class="margin-note note-c">no rounds through the pack</aside></div></div><div class="phase reveal" id="execution-phase-2" data-phase="2"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="2" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">PHASE 2 / 5</div><h3>Read the Ground</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Establish an OP over the hub. Identify the transmitter building, the generator, the alarm and air-watch position, and the crew-served positions on the wire. Cut the buried landline trunk so the hub can only be reached by radio - no cable cross-check when the false order goes out.</p></div><div class="phase reveal" id="execution-phase-3" data-phase="3"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="3" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">PHASE 3 / 5</div><h3>Take the Hub</h3><div class="annotated"><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Breach the perimeter and clear the position. This is the loud part of the night. The transmitter and encryption set are NOT to be demolished - Orion needs them working. Pull the signals log off the desk: current call-signs, authentication tables, and the convoy serial. Hold the position.</p><aside class="margin-note note-d">the box stays intact</aside></div></div><div class="phase reveal" id="execution-phase-4" data-phase="4"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="4" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">PHASE 4 / 5</div><h3>One Authenticated Order</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">With Volkov's keys, the log's current authentication, and a working transmitter, send one keyed false order in the corps' own format. Because it authenticates, the sector net acts on it. The order reroutes the staged convoy off its planned axis. Choose the content - this is the operation's fixed decision, and it colours the Russian starting positions in the finale:</p><ul class="reveal decrypt-scroll"><li><strong>Phantom FDF build-up</strong> - the convoy is pushed onto a longer northern route to avoid contact.</li><li><strong>False evacuation corridor</strong> - the convoy holds and reroutes to screen a civilian corridor that does not exist.</li><li><strong>False withdrawal order</strong> - the convoy pushes forward hard into ground it now believes is clear.</li></ul></div><div class="phase reveal" id="execution-phase-5" data-phase="5"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="5" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">PHASE 5 / 5</div><h3>Break Contact</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Exfil west off the ridge through the farmstead line and the level crossing while the sector is already redeploying - checkpoints shifting the wrong way because of the order Orion just sent.</p></div><div class="phase climax reveal" id="execution-climax" data-phase="6"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="6" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">COMBAT CLIMAX</div><h3>Your Own Order Comes Back</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">The hub missed a scheduled check-in and a QRF element is sweeping the likely egress routes. At the same time the head of the rerouted convoy is now moving along the axis that overlaps Orion's exfil. A moving fight over two to three points - break the manned level-crossing checkpoint, then slip past or punch through the lead vehicles of the convoy before it clears. No last room to clear. Just distance and timing.</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">The decision at the crossing: blow the transmitter before you leave - clean break, but the loss registers instantly and the deception has hours, not a day - or leave it standing and keyed, and the false order keeps propagating while a real corps transmission may get through and contradict it.</p></div><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll" style="color:var(--dim); font-size:12px;">Ground commanders retain discretionary authority over internal task allocation and approach across all phases.</p></div></section>
  <section id="roe" class="briefing-section"><h2 class="op-name">RULES OF ENGAGEMENT</h2><h3 class="op-title">FIELD RESTRICTIONS</h3><div class="intel reveal"><div class="head">ROE // EFFECTIVE IMMEDIATELY</div><div class="annotated"><ul class="reveal decrypt-scroll"><li>Any 44th Army Corps element observed, in contact, or confirmed at a designated objective is hostile.</li><li>Colonel Volkov is a capture-or-kill HVT. The key set matters more than the man - do not let a firefight put rounds through the fill device or burn the codebook.</li><li>The transmitter, encryption set, and signals log at the hub are mission-critical and are not to be destroyed before Phase 4 is complete.</li><li>Lethal force is authorised against confirmed hostile positions without further clearance. This is a direct-action operation, not a restrained security posture.</li><li>A journalist, Nieminen - freelance, persistent - is working the region. Orion is not officially present. Do not get photographed.</li><li>Self-defence is authorised at all times without prior command approval.</li></ul><aside class="margin-note note-e">copy that</aside></div></div></section>
  <section id="support" class="briefing-section"><h2 class="op-name">SUPPORT</h2><h3 class="op-title">AVAILABLE ASSETS</h3><div><div class="phase reveal"><div class="num">COMMS</div><h3>Recovered In-Mission</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">The FDF listening post at the treeline hands over the initial fix on Volkov's movement and the hub layout, then goes quiet - it will not acknowledge Orion on any net. Sector frequencies and the hub's authentication are not held at start; they are recovered in Phase 1 (keys) and Phase 3 (log).</p></div><div class="phase reveal"><div class="num">AIR SUPPORT</div><h3>Valkyrie</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Valkyrie provides limited CAS and overwatch in this sector on request through mission command. No standing air presence. No dedicated extraction airframe is assigned - plan the egress on the ground.</p></div></div></section>
  <section id="operator-note" class="operator-note reveal" aria-label="Operator's note"><div class="head">OFF-RECORD // FOR THE PERSON WHO READS TO THE END</div><p>You are not blowing this hub. You are going to fight your way into it, sit at someone else's desk, and tell their army a lie in their own handwriting.</p><p>Send it once. Then be a long way west before the sun comes up and someone reads it back.</p></section>
  <script>
    const unlockPhase = (phase: string) => {
      const blip = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(`.blip[data-phase="${phase}"]`);
      if (!blip) return;
      blip.classList.remove('locked');
      blip.removeAttribute('aria-hidden');
      blip.removeAttribute('tabindex');
    };
    document.querySelectorAll('.blip').forEach((blip) => blip.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const target = document.querySelector(blip.dataset.target || '');
      if (!(target instanceof HTMLElement) || blip.classList.contains('locked')) return;
      const reducedMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      target.scrollIntoView({ behavior: reducedMotion ? 'auto' : 'smooth', block: 'center' });
      target.classList.remove('flash');
      void target.offsetWidth;
      target.classList.add('flash');
      window.setTimeout(() => target.classList.remove('flash'), 1500);
    }));
    const phaseObserver = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (!entry.isIntersecting || !(entry.target instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
        const phase = entry.target.dataset.phase;
        if (!phase) return;
        unlockPhase(phase);
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.45 });
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.phase[data-phase]').forEach((phase) => phaseObserver.observe(phase));

    const checklistKey = 'orion-checklist-op2';
    const completePhases = new Set<number>(JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(checklistKey) || '[]'));
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-checklist-phase]').forEach((input) => {
      const phase = Number(input.dataset.checklistPhase);
      input.checked = completePhases.has(phase);
      input.addEventListener('change', () => {
        input.checked ? completePhases.add(phase) : completePhases.delete(phase);
        localStorage.setItem(checklistKey, JSON.stringify([...completePhases]));
      });
    });

    document.querySelector('.print-opord')?.addEventListener('click', () => window.print());
  </script>
</Layout>
